WEBVTT

00:12.595 --> 00:16.516
The Educational Rights Protection Bureau
has implemented mandatory urine tests

00:16.599 --> 00:18.268
for all students nationwide.

00:18.351 --> 00:21.521
The Bureau said this would provide
early detection and treatment

00:21.604 --> 00:25.275
of kidney abnormalities
and diabetes-related conditions.

00:25.358 --> 00:27.193
However, some are raising suspicions

00:27.277 --> 00:29.320
that the tests are actually
meant to screen for drugs

00:29.404 --> 00:31.031
that have been circulating in schools.

00:31.114 --> 00:34.409
Amid the controversy, several schools
have refused to participate,

00:34.492 --> 00:36.286
citing final exams.

00:36.369 --> 00:37.746
Seungyeon High School,

00:37.829 --> 00:40.790
known to be the most
academically competitive in Gangnam.

00:40.874 --> 00:43.501
It's also the school
that sends the most students in the nation

00:43.585 --> 00:45.336
to Seoul National University
Medical School.

00:45.420 --> 00:47.505
You said you lived around there.
Do you know about it?

00:48.131 --> 00:50.633
My family moved near that school
when I was seven

00:50.717 --> 00:52.927
because my mom wanted me to go there.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.512
Didn't you go to a science school?

00:55.096 --> 00:56.389
Yeah.

00:57.307 --> 00:58.767
Well, Seungyeon High students

00:58.850 --> 01:03.146
are said to have
extremely demanding parents behind them.

01:03.646 --> 01:06.149
CLASS S

01:09.903 --> 01:12.822
This is the last exam
you can take for early admissions.

01:12.906 --> 01:15.325
If you fail this,
the CSAT is your last hope.

01:15.408 --> 01:17.869
So, you'd better
do well on this one. All right?

01:17.952 --> 01:19.079
Yes, sir.

01:19.162 --> 01:20.663
Okay. Begin.

01:41.643 --> 01:44.521
Wow, Class 1, Class 2, and then Class S?

01:45.188 --> 01:46.147
I told you.

01:46.231 --> 01:48.817
This school sends more students
to med school than anywhere else.

01:49.609 --> 01:52.070
Everyone in that class
is aiming to go there.

01:53.822 --> 01:57.158
It's basically filled with
the top students in the whole school.

02:33.903 --> 02:35.530
My dear son!

02:37.448 --> 02:40.577
Look! Congratulations
on getting into med school, honey!

02:40.660 --> 02:42.704
Hey! That's awesome!

02:42.787 --> 02:44.247
Congrats!

02:44.330 --> 02:45.582
Yeah!

03:12.108 --> 03:14.986
-Wait! Who are you?
-Hey, are you okay

03:15.069 --> 03:17.488
The Educational Rights Protection Bureau.

03:30.835 --> 03:32.462
Oh! Oh, he's bleeding.

03:32.545 --> 03:35.256
Inspector, take him
to the nurse's office. Thanks.

03:35.340 --> 03:38.426
-I got you.
-Sir, where is the… the nurse's office?

03:38.509 --> 03:41.554
-Left and down the stairs.
-Left, then down. Thanks.

03:42.805 --> 03:43.640
Come on.

03:54.817 --> 03:55.860
-Oh.
-Careful.

03:55.944 --> 03:57.570
Support his neck. Ease him down.

04:10.291 --> 04:12.418
-Stop the exam right now!
-Done.

04:13.169 --> 04:14.963
My son isn't able to take it!

04:18.424 --> 04:20.927
It will literally kill us
if he can't take it.

04:21.552 --> 04:24.931
Are you going to take responsibility
for him not getting into med school?

04:25.014 --> 04:26.599
He is going to take that exam!

04:30.061 --> 04:33.523
-Where's Hyeon-min?!
-Ma'am, your son fainted during an exam.

04:34.899 --> 04:36.484
Did you finish the exam?

04:39.904 --> 04:43.366
It's okay. I talked to the teacher.
There's still time to finish it.

04:43.449 --> 04:45.368
You can get up, right? Let's do this.

04:46.953 --> 04:47.787
Uh…

04:48.830 --> 04:51.541
Ma, I don't feel so good.

04:51.624 --> 04:53.960
'Cause you stayed up all night studying.
Everyone did.

04:55.253 --> 04:56.129
Here.

04:57.297 --> 04:58.715
But, Mom,

04:59.340 --> 05:01.926
I keep having these weird thoughts.

05:02.010 --> 05:05.596
You're losing focus. That's why
you're having these weird thoughts.

05:06.973 --> 05:08.391
I've got your medicine.

05:09.392 --> 05:10.768
You'll feel better soon.

05:13.021 --> 05:14.022
Here.

05:18.109 --> 05:18.943
Drink.

05:25.199 --> 05:26.617
You're so close now.

05:28.244 --> 05:31.289
You don't want all of our hard work
to go to waste, do you?

05:32.165 --> 05:34.292
Don't give up, honey. I'm counting on you.

05:36.544 --> 05:37.545
Come on.

05:58.566 --> 06:02.653
TEACH YOU A LESSON

06:08.951 --> 06:10.286
Attention, students.

06:10.787 --> 06:14.665
We have a special directive from
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau.

06:14.749 --> 06:19.253
All students are to remain in school
and prepare to take urine tests.

06:25.718 --> 06:26.886
MY SON

06:30.932 --> 06:31.766
Hyeon-min.

06:31.849 --> 06:33.184
How'd the test go?

06:33.935 --> 06:35.395
You managed to do it all?

06:37.980 --> 06:38.856
Why?

06:40.066 --> 06:41.359
What do they want with you?

06:42.110 --> 06:43.486
They're nuts at the ERPB.

06:43.986 --> 06:44.904
Okay, son.

06:44.987 --> 06:47.490
I'll head to the school.
Call the other mothers.

06:47.573 --> 06:48.991
The Bureau's doing what?

06:49.075 --> 06:52.703
Oh my God! Are they out of their minds?
The kids are expected at the academy.

06:54.455 --> 06:57.375
-Want me to line them up?
-Where d'you think you're going?

06:58.000 --> 06:59.627
Didn't you hear about the test?

06:59.710 --> 07:01.087
We have somewhere to go.

07:01.170 --> 07:02.338
Go after the urine test.

07:02.422 --> 07:04.424
Our moms are coming.
You should talk to them.

07:04.507 --> 07:06.968
This is ridiculous. Are you kidding me?

07:07.051 --> 07:09.887
Da-hui, what are you doing?
You're going to be late.

07:11.347 --> 07:12.640
What's going on?

07:20.481 --> 07:22.984
Okay, ladies.
What do you think you're doing here?

07:23.067 --> 07:24.068
What are we doing?

07:24.152 --> 07:26.404
Hyeon-min's mom, please be quiet.

07:27.655 --> 07:30.992
Do you have any idea what a critical time
this is for the children?

07:31.826 --> 07:35.746
For top students, one point can mean
the difference between college admissions.

07:35.830 --> 07:39.667
We may not be armed, but the parents
and students here are at war.

07:40.251 --> 07:42.587
War? Is that why
you're willing to put lives on the line?

07:43.754 --> 07:47.216
I take it you've heard the rumors?
We'll be screening for drugs.

07:47.884 --> 07:51.345
For drugs? Are you suggesting
that our kids are addicts?

07:54.056 --> 07:57.101
Those kids are applying
to Seoul University med school.

07:57.185 --> 07:59.854
-They're not like other kids.
-They look alike to me.

08:01.814 --> 08:06.235
Listen, have you even considered
what it took to get our children here?

08:06.736 --> 08:10.281
From birth, through daycare,
elementary, middle and high school,

08:10.364 --> 08:13.284
all the way up to their senior
and most important year,

08:13.367 --> 08:15.036
they haven't wasted a second.

08:15.119 --> 08:19.790
Oh. And what about the moms here?
We sleep an hour less than our kids do.

08:19.874 --> 08:22.126
We wake up early,
send them to after-school academies,

08:22.210 --> 08:23.461
hire consultants and tutors.

08:24.587 --> 08:26.797
They can do the test after the CSAT.

08:27.298 --> 08:30.676
Whoever chooses to not take the test
will be penalized on their CSAT results.

08:30.760 --> 08:34.514
What? Penalized? Are you threatening
our children's livelihood?

08:34.597 --> 08:36.098
If I was, would you listen to me?

08:36.182 --> 08:39.894
This is Daechi-dong! You really think
you can take on the moms here?

08:39.977 --> 08:42.647
Yeah. The Bureau can handle it.

08:42.730 --> 08:45.858
Then go right ahead.
Try it and you'll see people die.

08:45.942 --> 08:48.110
We're doing this so people don't die.

08:48.194 --> 08:51.989
If we can save one before it's too late,
it'll be worth it.

08:54.784 --> 08:56.160
There's a hospital the ERPB uses.

08:56.244 --> 08:59.288
Bring your children there
before school tomorrow to get tested.

08:59.372 --> 09:00.540
If you don't,

09:02.124 --> 09:04.293
there will be serious consequences.

09:13.678 --> 09:15.304
You're Hyeon-min's mother, right?

09:17.473 --> 09:19.892
I saw him earlier.
He looked like he was in a bad way.

09:20.518 --> 09:22.353
Make sure you get him tested tomorrow.

09:36.075 --> 09:37.410
Do you

09:37.994 --> 09:39.495
have any idea who I am?

09:40.580 --> 09:42.957
Uh, I… I've seen you on television.

09:44.125 --> 09:46.794
-You're a very important person.
-Hm.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.173
I heard your hand was injured
because of the Bureau.

09:51.757 --> 09:53.134
Oh, uh, no. No.

09:53.217 --> 09:55.094
It was all my own doing.

09:55.177 --> 09:58.764
Listen. I'm not trying
to blame them at all.

09:59.265 --> 10:01.183
I just want to help you, Gyu-cheol.

10:02.560 --> 10:03.811
You do? Why?

10:04.687 --> 10:07.565
I like giving opportunities
to those in need.

10:08.065 --> 10:09.817
It's my job as a politician.

10:11.736 --> 10:13.738
Could I take a look at your hand?

10:15.698 --> 10:19.243
That doesn't look like a minor injury. You
should go to a hospital on the outside.

10:22.496 --> 10:26.751
An attack with a sharp weapon
occurred at a juvenile detention center.

10:26.834 --> 10:30.129
During a visit by the ERPB program
for underage offenders,

10:30.212 --> 10:32.548
an inmate at the facility
attacked one of them.

10:32.632 --> 10:35.217
It could have easily
resulted in serious injury or…

10:35.301 --> 10:36.594
-What?
-Oh. Nothing.

10:36.677 --> 10:39.347
…action of another inmate,
the juveniles were unharmed.

10:39.430 --> 10:42.642
People were shocked to hear, though,
that the inmate--

10:42.725 --> 10:45.102
-Where is it?
-Oh, over there, sir.

10:45.186 --> 10:46.771
-Lead the way. Come on.
-Yeah.

10:46.854 --> 10:49.440
When asked why they chose the facility…

10:49.523 --> 10:50.399
Uh, do you know--

10:50.483 --> 10:52.985
Will you stop? I'm even more aware of it
because of you.

10:53.069 --> 10:57.323
The whole thing was on TV earlier.
Don't sweat it. I saw.

10:57.406 --> 10:59.659
-Are you okay?
-Of course I'm not.

10:59.742 --> 11:02.078
Shit. Where the hell
did they get that photo?

11:02.578 --> 11:04.664
Are all the kids from the school
getting the test?

11:04.747 --> 11:05.956
Yes, they are, sir.

11:13.756 --> 11:16.300
Do you feel anxious? Let's go outside.

11:17.426 --> 11:19.053
Why do we have to do this?

11:24.350 --> 11:25.226
Drink this.

11:28.270 --> 11:30.189
Are you okay? Do you feel less anxious?

11:30.773 --> 11:32.149
Yeah. It's better here.

11:32.233 --> 11:33.401
Huh.

11:37.697 --> 11:40.032
REPORT CARDS WERE DISTRIBUTED
TO STUDENTS TODAY

11:41.200 --> 11:43.452
The report cards are out.
They emailed them.

11:43.536 --> 11:44.745
-Check yours.
-Oh.

11:50.292 --> 11:51.210
REPORT CARD

11:57.425 --> 12:00.428
That was the exam
I was doing when I passed out.

12:03.431 --> 12:04.682
I'm so sorry, Mom.

12:12.064 --> 12:13.607
What did I tell you?

12:15.818 --> 12:19.780
Kids like you who can't handle pressure
need to take their meds.

12:21.407 --> 12:23.492
Is it really that hard to take one pill?

12:25.244 --> 12:27.413
Don't you feel sorry for me at all?

12:28.205 --> 12:31.417
I've had to bow down to all the other moms
because of you.

12:33.210 --> 12:35.546
I'm not asking for anything else.

12:37.131 --> 12:39.133
All I want is for you to study!

12:42.052 --> 12:44.305
If you knew how hard I worked for you…

12:48.684 --> 12:49.518
Jesus.

13:20.883 --> 13:23.928
Our son's goal
is to attend SNU Med School.

13:25.012 --> 13:28.349
I hear you're one
of the top admissions consultants.

13:29.517 --> 13:33.270
Let's start by seeing what level he's at.
How far along is he academically?

13:34.480 --> 13:36.148
I had him study ahead.

13:36.649 --> 13:39.819
He's only in first year middle school,
but he's already doing high-school math.

13:39.902 --> 13:42.696
He hasn't finished it?
He's still doing high-school math?

13:44.240 --> 13:46.075
I'm sure he'll be done soon.

13:46.575 --> 13:48.702
He's top of his class right now.

13:48.786 --> 13:52.915
Top in a provincial school is the
equivalent of lower level in Gangnam.

13:53.499 --> 13:55.543
Don't even think about med school.

13:55.626 --> 13:56.460
Oh.

13:57.086 --> 13:59.463
We're not in the provinces.

13:59.547 --> 14:00.756
Seoul's right next door.

14:00.840 --> 14:02.716
You should meet my son first before--

14:02.800 --> 14:07.137
Do you know when the moms in Gangnam
start preparing their kids for med school?

14:08.931 --> 14:10.266
The moment they're born.

14:10.933 --> 14:13.811
They map out a 20-year plan,
from birth to med school.

14:13.894 --> 14:18.023
They choose the appropriate day cares,
schools, academies, and tutors.

14:18.107 --> 14:19.275
Those kids are ten years ahead

14:19.358 --> 14:22.945
of the ones who suddenly decided on
medicine when they were in middle school.

14:24.196 --> 14:27.741
At his age, Hyeon-min should have
already finished the CSAT curriculum

14:27.825 --> 14:32.079
and be doing non-stop practice questions
to avoid mistakes on the actual test.

14:32.580 --> 14:35.749
He should be prepping for
school interviews and working on essays.

14:37.126 --> 14:39.211
Do you see what I'm getting at here?

14:39.712 --> 14:40.963
He's quite far behind.

14:41.589 --> 14:44.049
Still, he can do it.

14:46.260 --> 14:50.639
Here are the problems the kids
in Daechi-dong are solving right now.

14:53.726 --> 14:56.353
How many do you think
Hyeon-min could answer?

15:16.040 --> 15:18.083
DAECHI SKY REAL ESTATE

15:20.044 --> 15:23.339
PRIME LISTING
A HOME THAT SENT KIDS TO SNU MED SCHOOL

15:23.422 --> 15:25.215
GRAND PRIZE IN ENGLISH, JUNG HYEON-MIN

15:26.508 --> 15:29.053
Do we really have to live in this place?

15:29.803 --> 15:32.765
It's walking distance
to the academy and school.

15:32.848 --> 15:34.558
It's Gangnam, so that's a plus.

15:34.642 --> 15:38.270
And also, two boys
who went to SNU Med School lived here.

15:38.771 --> 15:42.066
-Didn't have to pay a deposit either.
-I don't know.

15:42.566 --> 15:45.653
A school's a school.
What's so special about the ones here?

15:45.736 --> 15:47.237
What are you talking about?

15:47.321 --> 15:50.532
The school has a special class
for seniors aiming for med school.

15:50.616 --> 15:54.286
If you manage to get in there, you're
pretty much guaranteed to go to SNU.

15:54.370 --> 15:56.747
Hyeon-min's goal is
to get into that class.

15:57.873 --> 16:01.168
Yeah, but still, this place is so…

16:01.669 --> 16:05.631
Don't you want this for him?
Your younger brother went to med school.

16:05.714 --> 16:08.425
Your family doesn't treat you
the same way they treat him, do they?

16:08.509 --> 16:11.804
But it's thanks to him
I, uh, got that job at the hospital.

16:11.887 --> 16:14.223
We should be happy. Grateful.

16:14.306 --> 16:16.225
That's exactly why
you get treated like that.

16:16.308 --> 16:19.561
Why I get treated like that.
Same with Hyeon-min. I'm tired of it.

16:19.645 --> 16:23.315
I'm gonna make sure he gets
into med school. No one'll look down then.

16:23.399 --> 16:24.984
Who's looking down on him now?

16:25.067 --> 16:27.069
Ugh, cut it out!

16:27.569 --> 16:31.240
Stop ruining this moment
and just take the door off!

16:31.740 --> 16:33.158
Ugh. Okay, okay.

16:36.203 --> 16:37.579
Grab that side. You got it?

16:38.080 --> 16:39.581
Okay, okay. Keep holding on.

16:46.630 --> 16:49.383
GOAL
GET INTO SEUNGYEON HIGH!

16:53.012 --> 16:56.682
GOAL
GET INTO SNU MEDICAL SCHOOL!

17:11.905 --> 17:12.740
Here.

17:13.866 --> 17:16.118
I'm not being unreasonable, you know.

17:16.618 --> 17:18.245
All the moms here are like this.

17:19.747 --> 17:20.748
Okay.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.209
Uh, Mom, what about the tutor?

17:24.293 --> 17:27.796
It looks like all the other kids
have the same one.

17:28.714 --> 17:31.383
I'm looking into it. Don't you worry.

17:31.467 --> 17:32.509
Back to work.

17:40.100 --> 17:43.479
Could you please invite me
to the next moms' meeting?

17:50.027 --> 17:51.570
Hey. Here you go.

17:52.196 --> 17:53.739
-Your tea.
-Mm.

17:53.822 --> 17:56.450
Forget about all the other moms.

17:56.533 --> 17:59.244
You wanna make sure
you're on Da-hui's mom's good side.

17:59.328 --> 18:01.705
-She's the big mama pig. Know what I mean?
-The mama pig?

18:01.789 --> 18:04.666
You know how a sow
always has her piglets trailing after her?

18:04.750 --> 18:07.586
She's mama pig
to all the mothers that trail after her.

18:10.923 --> 18:12.674
Ah, but, um,

18:13.175 --> 18:14.510
not just anyone can do it.

18:14.593 --> 18:16.970
Information is power with the moms here.

18:17.054 --> 18:19.807
Da-hui's mom has all the connections.

18:19.890 --> 18:23.018
Tutoring coordinators,
admission consultants,

18:23.102 --> 18:27.397
and even academies with programs
geared toward SNU Med School.

18:27.481 --> 18:29.691
You're not a working mom, are you?

18:29.775 --> 18:32.486
No, I'm not. Uh, why do you ask?

18:32.569 --> 18:37.199
Working moms and dual-income parents
don't make it into this inner circle.

18:37.282 --> 18:40.994
They just take the info and run,
acting all busy and whatever.

18:41.078 --> 18:44.373
But doctors and professors?
They get a major pass.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.208
Why do they get one?

18:46.291 --> 18:49.837
For early admission, you've gotta build up
their student record.

18:49.920 --> 18:51.755
Volunteering at the hospital,

18:51.839 --> 18:54.049
doing lab research at the university.

18:54.133 --> 18:56.301
That's what looks best
on a student record.

18:56.385 --> 18:59.138
On top of that,
if Da-hui's mom's on your side, it's done.

19:00.889 --> 19:03.642
So I really have to stay on her good side.

19:03.725 --> 19:05.102
Of course!

19:13.402 --> 19:15.279
It's not time for bed yet.

19:15.362 --> 19:16.446
I'm sorry.

19:16.947 --> 19:19.783
-I'm just tired.
-I know you are. Eat while you study.

19:22.077 --> 19:24.121
Can I have a little more, please?

19:24.204 --> 19:27.541
If you eat too much food,
you'll become even more sleepy.

19:27.624 --> 19:32.337
A little glucose is all the brain needs.
Just eat this and focus more. Hm?

19:40.596 --> 19:42.097
Oh, hi, my love.

19:44.141 --> 19:47.352
Look, we're living here,
and you're there all by yourself.

19:47.436 --> 19:51.231
You should either move to a cheaper
studio apartment or in with your mother.

19:51.315 --> 19:52.816
STUDY SCHEDULE
3 HOURS' SLEEP A DAY

19:52.900 --> 19:55.068
I'm doing this for Hyeon-min!

20:00.407 --> 20:02.075
It'll all be worth it.

20:02.701 --> 20:04.161
When he's a doctor, you'll see.

20:19.676 --> 20:21.929
I didn't want to come empty-handed.

20:22.429 --> 20:23.388
I hope you like it.

20:25.724 --> 20:27.851
You shouldn't have.

20:32.731 --> 20:35.067
Listen, I came here to see you, because--

20:35.150 --> 20:37.402
Every mom comes to see me
for the same reason.

20:37.486 --> 20:39.613
Yeong-jun's mom already told me about you.

20:40.948 --> 20:43.992
Why don't you come to a few
of our meetings and see how it goes?

20:46.119 --> 20:47.079
Okay.

20:47.579 --> 20:49.164
3 MANGO JUICES, 1 APPLE ADE

20:49.748 --> 20:51.208
-That's good.
-What would you like?

20:51.291 --> 20:53.460
-Oh, I'll have an iced latte.
-Iced latte.

20:53.543 --> 20:55.921
-Double shot, please.
-Double shot.

20:56.630 --> 20:57.547
Double shot.

20:58.715 --> 21:01.176
-Too much.
-It's just getting started.

21:02.261 --> 21:05.013
-Here we are. Your iced latte.
-Thank you.

21:05.097 --> 21:07.683
-She's naturally gifted.
-Of course. It's Da-hui.

21:07.766 --> 21:12.854
She wouldn't be at that level otherwise.
For math, the finest tutor is Jung Da-eun.

21:13.355 --> 21:16.024
She's famous for sending kids to SNU Med.

21:16.566 --> 21:18.819
Her one downside
is her academic background.

21:20.153 --> 21:23.907
As for English, the one to go with
is Oh Bo-hyeon.

21:25.742 --> 21:27.661
ENGLISH
OH BO-HYEON

21:31.039 --> 21:33.834
It's easier if you start
with the cube root of 27.

21:34.835 --> 21:38.213
You know that's three, right?
Now, what's 15 times 6?

21:38.297 --> 21:39.965
-Ninety.
-That's very good.

21:40.549 --> 21:43.427
It's 90.
Now why don't you try solving this one?

21:43.510 --> 21:45.220
REPORT CARD
GRADE 1, SEMESTER 1, 2024

22:03.572 --> 22:04.489
Don't worry.

22:04.990 --> 22:07.367
A child's grades
depends on the parent's effort.

22:07.451 --> 22:08.327
Hm?

22:16.293 --> 22:17.544
Jeez.

22:20.714 --> 22:25.260
It turns out these plates
come as a set. I wish I'd known.

22:25.344 --> 22:27.971
I would have brought
the whole thing last time.

22:28.055 --> 22:29.890
You shouldn't have.

22:30.390 --> 22:33.018
I heard about Hyeon-min.

22:33.101 --> 22:35.812
He didn't get into med school prep class
this time either, right?

22:35.896 --> 22:38.732
Well, I did get him
that tutor you recommended,

22:38.815 --> 22:42.402
and he goes to the same academy
as Da-hui attends.

22:42.486 --> 22:44.613
I honestly don't know what else to do.

22:44.696 --> 22:48.200
Just sitting at a desk all day long
doesn't mean a kid knows how to study.

22:48.283 --> 22:50.160
Two kids can study the same thing
for an hour.

22:50.744 --> 22:54.706
One walks away knowing all of it.
The other only gets about half.

22:55.415 --> 22:56.958
That's because he wasn't focusing.

22:58.085 --> 23:00.504
Is there a tutor
to help with that as well?

23:03.340 --> 23:06.593
There are some things a tutor
can help with, and some they can't.

23:09.721 --> 23:10.806
Just a minute.

23:22.776 --> 23:25.070
Here you go. Give him this.

23:25.570 --> 23:27.906
It'll make a huge difference in his focus.

23:27.989 --> 23:31.618
I gave it to Da-hui,
and her grades really went up.

23:32.869 --> 23:33.745
Huh.

23:55.725 --> 23:56.601
Hyeon-min.

23:58.353 --> 23:59.271
Uh-huh?

23:59.354 --> 24:02.232
I went through a lot of hoops
to get this for you, honey.

24:02.315 --> 24:03.733
It's gonna help you study.

24:04.317 --> 24:07.612
I know you would do really well
if you could just focus more.

24:07.696 --> 24:09.322
Everyone says this stuff is great.

24:09.406 --> 24:12.409
It helps you focus,
and you won't get nervous during exams.

24:13.368 --> 24:15.454
All the kids around here are taking it.

24:24.796 --> 24:25.630
Go on, then.

24:29.718 --> 24:31.511
This is an illegal drug.

24:34.014 --> 24:35.891
Judging by your faces, you knew that.

24:36.475 --> 24:39.853
It's a medication for ADHD
that hasn't been approved in this country.

24:39.936 --> 24:43.607
It's been quietly shared among mothers
because it's said to improve focus.

24:43.690 --> 24:44.858
You're all aware of that.

24:45.358 --> 24:47.944
I know you are, so here we go.

24:48.612 --> 24:50.739
The children's urine tests

24:50.822 --> 24:52.449
came back positive

24:52.532 --> 24:55.702
for methylphenidate and atomoxetine.

24:55.785 --> 24:59.164
These two drugs are only prescribed
together in extremely rare cases,

24:59.247 --> 25:00.790
and for high-risk patients.

25:00.874 --> 25:03.168
In particular, methylphenidate.

25:03.251 --> 25:06.755
It is classified here
as a controlled psychotropic substance

25:06.838 --> 25:08.423
under the Narcotics Control Act.

25:08.507 --> 25:13.011
Which means that taking it
without a prescription is illegal.

25:13.512 --> 25:16.848
It's a violation of both
the Pharmaceutical Affairs Act

25:16.932 --> 25:20.602
and the Narcotics Control Act,
so that makes it a criminal offense.

25:21.228 --> 25:22.062
It's okay.

25:22.145 --> 25:24.523
I'm afraid everyone here…

25:24.606 --> 25:26.525
…will have to be questioned by the police.

25:29.569 --> 25:31.238
-Inspector?
-Yeah?

25:31.738 --> 25:35.158
The test results for Jung Hyeon-min
are quite serious.

25:35.659 --> 25:36.660
Hyeon-min's mom.

25:38.411 --> 25:40.497
Has anyone seen Hyeon-min's mom?

25:40.580 --> 25:43.583
-Where'd she go?
-She went out that way.

25:45.460 --> 25:47.504
I heard your son's grades have gone up.

25:48.797 --> 25:52.884
Yes, something must have really clicked
inside him. He's totally changed.

25:52.968 --> 25:55.053
His focus has improved immensely.

25:55.136 --> 25:57.806
I think he'll be joining
the med school prep class soon.

25:58.515 --> 26:00.934
The competition is still brutal, you know?

26:01.434 --> 26:03.520
Do you know of any stronger medication

26:03.603 --> 26:06.314
than the one you gave me before?

26:06.398 --> 26:11.027
Well, I suppose I could look into it,
but that one should be enough.

26:15.615 --> 26:19.035
My son's grades improved
after taking ADHD medication.

26:19.119 --> 26:21.454
I'm looking for something
a little stronger.

26:21.538 --> 26:23.707
If anyone knows of something, please help.

26:24.416 --> 26:27.419
There's a medication
that helps improve grades? What is it?

26:27.502 --> 26:29.921
-Jeez, these are no help.
-I wanna know too!

26:33.883 --> 26:37.012
I have the meds
that last year's top student took.

26:37.095 --> 26:38.013
Want some?

27:06.041 --> 27:08.043
You're from the mom group, right?

27:08.835 --> 27:09.836
Yeah.

27:35.070 --> 27:38.198
TIER: 1

27:42.661 --> 27:45.246
So, you're happy?

27:45.747 --> 27:48.083
That's awesome! Oh, honey!

27:49.709 --> 27:51.419
Can you get into prep class now?

27:51.503 --> 27:54.297
Yeah. They told me
I could start going tomorrow.

27:57.509 --> 28:00.011
Yes! Oh!

28:00.637 --> 28:01.888
Good job, Son!

28:12.190 --> 28:13.692
JUNG HYEON-MIN'S MOTHER

28:13.775 --> 28:15.777
Sir, she's still not picking up.

28:15.860 --> 28:18.947
They found something other than ADHD meds
in her son's urine test.

28:19.030 --> 28:21.533
-It's a substance found in heart pills.
-What?

28:23.493 --> 28:25.495
The amount is close to a lethal dose.

28:26.746 --> 28:30.166
If he keeps taking it, or increases
the dose, it could be life-threatening.

28:30.250 --> 28:31.876
-Am I right?
-Yes, you are.

28:31.960 --> 28:33.128
He's right?! What?

28:33.628 --> 28:35.338
Then why don't you speed up?

28:35.422 --> 28:36.631
I will! Okay, fine!

28:44.931 --> 28:45.932
Hyeon-min,

28:46.850 --> 28:48.017
it's not your fault.

28:49.185 --> 28:50.603
It's just a bit of bad luck.

28:50.687 --> 28:53.565
Early admission is gone,
but you'll still have the CSAT.

28:53.648 --> 28:55.942
If you do well,
you still get into med school.

28:59.320 --> 29:01.823
Son, you just need
to pull yourself together, okay?

29:03.158 --> 29:06.411
I'll tell the school
that you'll be working from home.

29:06.911 --> 29:09.873
You can study here
for the CSAT. All right?

29:15.462 --> 29:16.629
Um, Ma,

29:18.131 --> 29:19.883
get me the fucking meds.

29:21.301 --> 29:22.302
You got it.

29:22.802 --> 29:24.179
I'll go get them right now.

29:43.448 --> 29:44.532
Hyeon-min!

29:46.075 --> 29:47.285
Open the door!

29:51.748 --> 29:53.041
Are you in there?

30:16.231 --> 30:18.983
-They won't open the door.
-Okay, got it, sir.

30:20.777 --> 30:22.946
-What did he say?
-They won't open the door.

30:24.823 --> 30:28.868
Th… this looks way too dangerous to me.
You're… you're not gonna jump, are you?

30:28.952 --> 30:31.204
-The kid could die if I don't.
-What?

30:35.667 --> 30:36.501
Whoa!

30:36.584 --> 30:38.002
Get down from there!

30:38.503 --> 30:39.838
Hold on tight, okay?

30:41.381 --> 30:42.799
Oh! Oh!

30:44.175 --> 30:45.468
Oh! You okay?

30:45.552 --> 30:48.429
Like I never left
With no ring rust 

30:48.513 --> 30:51.057
Nobody get the job done
Like the king does

30:51.140 --> 30:53.643
Feel that quick rush
Running through your veins

30:53.726 --> 30:56.521
It's insane how I keep going
Yeah, we maintain

30:56.604 --> 30:59.816
Back like I never left
With no ring rust

30:59.899 --> 31:02.569
Nobody get the job done
Like the king does…

31:05.905 --> 31:07.824
-Wait! Stop it, just wait!
-Give me!

31:07.907 --> 31:10.535
Not now. The ERPB is here.

31:22.088 --> 31:25.466
Inspector, Han-rim! Oh!
Oh, are you all right?

31:25.550 --> 31:27.093
Whoa.

31:27.176 --> 31:29.095
-Hyeon-min!
-No! Let go!

31:29.178 --> 31:31.347
-Don't! Stop!
-I want my pills!

31:31.431 --> 31:32.599
-Let it go!
-Oh!

31:33.182 --> 31:35.518
-No, no, no!
-Take him to hospital right now.

31:35.602 --> 31:36.644
Yes, sir!

31:38.062 --> 31:39.522
No! Wait! No!

31:40.106 --> 31:42.567
Hyeon-min! Let go of him. Hyeon-min!

31:43.067 --> 31:45.612
Stop! I want my son. Bring him back!

31:48.531 --> 31:50.700
Hyeon-min! Where are you taking him?

31:52.660 --> 31:55.246
Ma'am, do you know
what kind of medication this is?

31:56.581 --> 31:59.334
Some students call it
something that keeps you awake.

31:59.417 --> 32:02.086
Something that helps you focus.
The ADHD pill.

32:02.170 --> 32:05.840
Something that improves your grades.
Something that gets you into med school.

32:05.924 --> 32:06.966
We call it

32:07.467 --> 32:09.302
something that kills kids.

32:10.845 --> 32:12.430
It's an addictive drug.

32:15.516 --> 32:16.726
It's a drug?

32:16.809 --> 32:17.894
You didn't know?

32:19.562 --> 32:20.563
No, I didn't.

32:21.147 --> 32:24.067
I gave it to him because I heard
it helped with concentration.

32:24.150 --> 32:26.986
-You honestly weren't aware?
-How was I supposed to know?

32:27.070 --> 32:29.614
This is the first I'm hearing of it.
That it's a bad thing!

32:29.697 --> 32:31.324
You really didn't know?

32:32.241 --> 32:35.161
Hyeon-min showed no change in behavior
after taking it?

32:36.829 --> 32:38.289
You didn't notice anything?

32:47.340 --> 32:48.216
Hyeon-min?

32:53.137 --> 32:54.889
Oh. Oh!

32:54.973 --> 32:57.058
Oh my God. I'll pinch it for you.

32:59.268 --> 33:01.020
I WANT TO DIE

33:01.104 --> 33:03.189
You knew that drug was destroying him.

33:03.898 --> 33:05.191
You knew very well.

33:25.044 --> 33:28.589
Was this all because of med school?
You want him to get in that bad?

33:29.590 --> 33:32.260
You thought it was okay
to pump him full of drugs like this?

33:33.636 --> 33:36.097
I was only going to give it to him
until the CSAT.

33:36.180 --> 33:38.975
Things could go
very wrong for him before that.

33:39.058 --> 33:41.477
Med school's more important
than your son's life?

33:46.566 --> 33:48.443
I guess it seems to be.

33:49.277 --> 33:50.945
He's almost there, though!

33:51.529 --> 33:53.197
Every second counts now.

33:53.281 --> 33:56.617
He doesn't have any time for this.
My son needs to study!

33:57.326 --> 34:01.080
From now on, you are strictly forbidden
from leaving this apartment.

34:01.164 --> 34:05.376
-You can't do this. This is my home!
-This is for your son's protection.

34:05.460 --> 34:09.255
The Bureau's job is to separate
the child abuse offender from the victim.

34:09.338 --> 34:10.882
I'm no child abuser.

34:11.382 --> 34:13.593
I'm his mother, damn you!

34:13.676 --> 34:16.763
It's the most important
time of his life right now!

34:17.764 --> 34:19.140
If he doesn't get in,

34:19.223 --> 34:21.476
are you going to take the blame?

34:28.107 --> 34:30.234
If you want med school that badly,

34:32.111 --> 34:33.321
then go yourself.

34:46.793 --> 34:48.294
Hye… Hyeon-min, are you okay?

34:51.214 --> 34:52.799
Whoa!

34:54.050 --> 34:56.177
Stop! What are you doing?

34:57.804 --> 34:58.805
-Come on.
-It's okay.

34:58.888 --> 35:00.181
Come on.

35:02.350 --> 35:05.269
You can't handle pain.
Why'd you put your hand there?

35:06.437 --> 35:09.065
I'd rather hurt my hand
than see him hurt his head.

35:12.944 --> 35:15.404
You feel okay? You seem different.

35:18.241 --> 35:22.370
When I look at Hyeon-min,
it's like I'm looking at a younger me.

35:22.954 --> 35:26.582
-My mom wanted me to go to med school too.
-So, why didn't you?

35:26.666 --> 35:29.001
Because it was no fun at all.

35:38.719 --> 35:40.680
CSAT PREP
SAMPLE QUESTIONS

35:43.015 --> 35:44.684
What are you trying to do?

35:44.767 --> 35:45.935
I told you.

35:46.811 --> 35:48.813
If you want med school, then you go.

35:49.313 --> 35:51.607
Do you know
why I want Hyeon-min to go there?

35:52.650 --> 35:56.070
I've got no inheritance to give him.
No connections or backing.

35:56.737 --> 35:59.740
Kids who have to compete to get places
end up resenting their parents.

35:59.824 --> 36:03.119
Exactly. That's why
you should go to med school yourself.

36:03.202 --> 36:05.454
Then you can be
his connections and backing.

36:06.789 --> 36:10.209
Why are you putting all the burden on him?
I'm sure he'd rather learn from you.

36:10.293 --> 36:12.044
I can't go to med school. I'm too old!

36:13.004 --> 36:15.006
I think you can if you stick to this.

36:16.507 --> 36:17.383
Here.

36:19.468 --> 36:23.014
The study plan and meal schedule
you made for Hyeon-min.

36:23.097 --> 36:25.516
You did an excellent job on it.

36:25.600 --> 36:29.645
If you stick to these plans,
you should get into med school no problem.

36:33.107 --> 36:34.108
Start studying.

36:34.692 --> 36:38.446
When your practice exam scores are higher
than the med school cut-off ones,

36:38.529 --> 36:40.615
I'll permit you to see Hyeon-min.

36:42.283 --> 36:43.451
Ugh, shit!

36:43.951 --> 36:46.621
5:30 p.m.,
instead of after-school academy,

36:46.704 --> 36:50.166
complete at least three
CSAT English sections from past exams.

36:52.501 --> 36:55.046
If you get even one question wrong,
start over.

37:02.303 --> 37:04.347
It's not dinner time yet.

37:04.972 --> 37:07.099
Nutritional support for brain function.

37:07.183 --> 37:08.142
What's that?

37:08.226 --> 37:11.604
It's your supper.
You get tired when you're full.

37:12.230 --> 37:14.565
Ah, I'm just following
that meal plan you made.

37:20.613 --> 37:23.324
-I'll take it away if you don't eat them.
-I will.

37:23.407 --> 37:24.367
Ah.

37:29.455 --> 37:32.708
Watch online lectures,
fill out the daily error log,

37:33.209 --> 37:34.710
then sleep at 1 a.m.

37:39.048 --> 37:40.716
Time to wake up now.

37:43.886 --> 37:45.346
Let me sleep longer.

37:45.429 --> 37:48.057
Get up or fail!

37:48.641 --> 37:50.017
Ugh! Stop!

37:51.769 --> 37:52.728
No!

37:53.312 --> 37:55.273
What the heck are you doing? Jeez!

37:55.356 --> 37:57.858
This bed is getting in the way
of studying. I'll toss it.

37:57.942 --> 38:00.027
That's why you got rid of the door, right?

38:00.111 --> 38:01.946
Are you insane?!

38:02.029 --> 38:05.574
Insane? Can't you see
that I'm sacrificing myself for you here?

38:05.658 --> 38:07.618
You're not. You're just joking around.

38:08.494 --> 38:09.996
You think this is a joke?

38:10.621 --> 38:12.832
I'm giving you
the mirror treatment for fun?

38:12.915 --> 38:14.250
One day, I'll turn around and say,

38:14.333 --> 38:17.003
"All right, you've learned your lesson.
You can see your son."

38:17.670 --> 38:19.213
Is that what you think?

38:22.383 --> 38:24.135
That is never

38:25.344 --> 38:27.263
going to happen.

38:29.473 --> 38:32.977
There's only one way
you're gonna be able to get out of here.

38:34.520 --> 38:36.814
When you pass the CSAT.

38:56.584 --> 38:57.877
Oh. You're awake.

38:58.377 --> 38:59.545
How are you feeling?

39:01.505 --> 39:02.798
I'm sorry, man.

39:03.299 --> 39:04.258
Hm?

39:05.509 --> 39:06.927
You got hurt because of me.

39:08.804 --> 39:09.638
It's fine.

39:12.308 --> 39:13.267
Whoa.

39:14.310 --> 39:15.519
Easy.

39:17.021 --> 39:17.897
Hey.

39:19.690 --> 39:21.525
Can you get some of those pills for me?

39:22.318 --> 39:23.444
No, I can't.

39:24.153 --> 39:25.237
They're bad for you.

39:26.864 --> 39:28.449
They're bad for me?

39:28.532 --> 39:29.575
It's a drug.

39:35.706 --> 39:37.041
-Just one.
-I can't.

39:37.124 --> 39:40.544
One. I promise I'll never take it again.
I feel like I'll die without it!

39:40.628 --> 39:41.921
No! I said, no!

39:42.421 --> 39:44.048
You think you can control it?

39:45.049 --> 39:48.761
Everyone says they just need one.
That turns into "just one more."

39:48.844 --> 39:50.596
"Just one more" is too much.

39:50.679 --> 39:53.140
It ruins your body. Your mind too.

39:54.308 --> 39:55.601
Your entire life.

39:59.772 --> 40:02.942
If you want to survive this,
you've gotta stick it out.

40:20.334 --> 40:21.335
You failed.

40:31.470 --> 40:32.680
Failed again.

40:33.222 --> 40:34.306
Your score went up a bit.

40:36.392 --> 40:37.393
But you failed.

40:42.481 --> 40:47.528
Where the endless sky meets the sea 

40:50.239 --> 40:55.703
To where the echoes fade away

40:58.497 --> 41:02.042
I've given all I had to give

41:02.126 --> 41:05.713
Now I'll find the space

41:06.630 --> 41:11.927
Where my peace belongs

41:12.011 --> 41:14.763
STUDY SCHEDULE
JUST ONE MORE YEAR. YOU CAN DO THIS, SON

41:14.847 --> 41:17.683
GOAL
GET INTO SNU MED SCHOOL!

41:21.145 --> 41:23.230
I WANT TO DIE

41:30.905 --> 41:34.283
The love I've carried

41:34.783 --> 41:36.619
I'll never…

41:36.702 --> 41:38.204
I wanted to die.

41:39.330 --> 41:41.707
Felt like I was in a living hell,

41:41.790 --> 41:44.126
and it wouldn't end
until I got into that school.

41:46.629 --> 41:48.130
Let me go…

41:50.549 --> 41:52.301
Every time I felt like that,

41:52.384 --> 41:53.761
the pills helped.

41:58.641 --> 41:59.475
Mom?

42:00.601 --> 42:02.478
Can I please skip academy today?

42:03.646 --> 42:05.481
Why? What's wrong now?

42:06.065 --> 42:08.776
The ones who don't give up
are the happiest in the end.

42:08.859 --> 42:10.194
You can do it, honey.

42:11.779 --> 42:15.699
But in my heart, I feel no fear

42:15.783 --> 42:19.787
I leave behind the weight of time

42:19.870 --> 42:21.747
And drift beyond

42:21.830 --> 42:27.670
The stars that shine

42:50.651 --> 42:52.027
Why didn't you go?

42:56.323 --> 42:57.449
I'm sorry.

43:21.807 --> 43:23.642
When I took those pills Mom got me,

43:23.726 --> 43:25.811
I didn't want to die anymore.

43:28.022 --> 43:29.690
It didn't last long though.

43:30.399 --> 43:33.068
Pretty soon after,
that feeling came back again.

43:33.152 --> 43:34.111
I WANT TO DIE

43:34.695 --> 43:37.031
Can you please get me stronger ones?

43:39.575 --> 43:40.451
Hm.

43:41.994 --> 43:44.705
I took those pills because

43:45.205 --> 43:46.332
I didn't want to die.

43:46.415 --> 43:47.791
I wanted to live.

43:50.753 --> 43:52.546
Quit doing those pills, okay?

43:53.839 --> 43:56.717
Them, and anything else
that makes you feel like you want to die.

43:57.801 --> 44:00.763
If it's studying, then quit it too.

44:01.889 --> 44:04.350
If it's med school, you can quit it.

44:05.851 --> 44:07.102
If it's your mom, well,

44:07.603 --> 44:08.854
quit your mom too.

44:15.778 --> 44:17.404
How can I quit her?

44:20.741 --> 44:22.117
You did good.

44:23.410 --> 44:25.788
I guess that's too far.

44:27.706 --> 44:28.707
Sorry.

44:44.932 --> 44:48.018
Code's my birthday.
Do you know when it is?

44:52.856 --> 44:54.191
Let me out of here.

44:54.274 --> 44:56.318
It's too hard. I can't do it.

44:56.402 --> 44:58.654
So, when it gets too hard,
you get to quit?

44:59.488 --> 45:01.073
You never told your son he could do that.

45:01.156 --> 45:04.493
Do you honestly think
I was trying to kill my son?

45:04.576 --> 45:08.163
I sold a really lovely home
and moved into this awful place.

45:08.247 --> 45:11.750
I played servant to those moms
just to get any information I could.

45:11.834 --> 45:14.169
I woke up early every morning
to make him breakfast.

45:14.753 --> 45:18.841
I've never done anything for myself.
I don't even have a hobby. Nothing!

45:18.924 --> 45:20.843
Because I've got to pay his academy fees.

45:20.926 --> 45:24.930
I did all that, sacrificing everything,
so he could do well!

45:27.266 --> 45:30.602
You didn't sacrifice yourself
for your son.

45:31.103 --> 45:32.980
Hyeon-min has…

45:35.649 --> 45:38.110
sacrificed himself for you.

45:46.910 --> 45:48.203
DRAW YOUR DREAM JOB

45:50.497 --> 45:52.124
NAME: JUNG HYEON-MIN
DREAM: DOCTOR

45:55.377 --> 45:58.464
Oh, Hyeon-min, Mommy would be so happy
if you became a doctor.

45:58.547 --> 46:00.007
Yeah?

46:00.090 --> 46:01.383
Yes, I would.

46:01.467 --> 46:03.927
WHAT IS YOUR FUTURE SELF?

46:04.720 --> 46:08.807
You should become a doctor so you can
treat me whenever I'm sick, right?

46:08.891 --> 46:09.933
Mm-hmm.

46:11.935 --> 46:13.270
Doctor.

46:13.937 --> 46:17.483
Hyeon-min, you're such
a good boy. You always listen to me.

46:18.108 --> 46:19.067
Yeah.

46:22.529 --> 46:24.907
Don't you feel bad for me and your dad?

46:25.699 --> 46:27.785
Why do you think we're living like this?

46:27.868 --> 46:29.453
We're sacrificing it all!

46:30.704 --> 46:31.705
Just for you!

46:31.789 --> 46:33.624
This is all for you!

46:37.294 --> 46:38.587
Come on, Hyeon-min!

46:40.255 --> 46:41.465
You think I like this?

46:41.548 --> 46:44.426
It's hard for me, too,
but I'm putting up with it for you!

46:44.510 --> 46:45.677
Mom, I'm so sorry.

46:45.761 --> 46:48.430
I could be doing anything I wanted
if I wasn't stuck here.

46:48.514 --> 46:50.390
I'm sacrificing everything for you!

46:57.189 --> 46:59.191
I have to become a doctor.

46:59.274 --> 47:01.735
My mother's said that to me
since I was little.

47:02.945 --> 47:05.948
So I guess I just figured
that's what I was supposed to do.

47:13.121 --> 47:14.456
Stupid, huh?

47:19.336 --> 47:21.588
Hey. You did well in school, right?

47:21.672 --> 47:23.882
Huh? Nah, not really.

47:24.716 --> 47:27.177
Well, can you tell me
what I'm supposed to do now?

47:27.970 --> 47:28.929
Hm?

47:30.639 --> 47:34.142
First, think about the things
you like doing the most.

47:35.477 --> 47:38.564
I'm really happy
when I'm doing something I enjoy doing.

47:40.691 --> 47:43.944
I can tell you
a million things that my mom likes.

47:45.320 --> 47:47.489
But I can't think
of a single thing that I like.

47:49.032 --> 47:50.367
What do I like?

47:54.788 --> 47:58.041
There are a lot of options.
We'll figure it out together.

47:58.625 --> 47:59.960
You too, Inspector Im.

48:03.297 --> 48:04.339
Just come on.

48:05.048 --> 48:06.216
Give me a second. Okay?

48:06.300 --> 48:08.302
Hi. I talked to you about the books.

48:08.385 --> 48:11.054
-Yeah, yeah.
-Pediatric Center? What the…

48:14.057 --> 48:15.058
Ah.

48:18.937 --> 48:19.938
Look at these books.

48:20.022 --> 48:21.148
KANG WON-MI THE JUDO GIRL

48:21.231 --> 48:22.482
Hyeon-min's not a kid.

48:22.566 --> 48:27.112
I know. Here, you can read this,
and you read those.

48:27.613 --> 48:29.114
-Come on.
-But why?

48:29.865 --> 48:32.618
You actually want me to…
to read this thing right now?

48:32.701 --> 48:34.786
HAMSTER YAMMA WHO BECAME A YOUTUBER

48:40.918 --> 48:42.628
CHOI THE FIREFIGHTER CAT

48:47.299 --> 48:51.595
Your eyes 

48:51.678 --> 48:55.557
Still glowing 

48:56.058 --> 49:01.480
Just like the day we met 

49:02.731 --> 49:07.486
Your eyes 

49:07.569 --> 49:11.198
Still holding

49:11.740 --> 49:17.621
The light of our first day

49:17.704 --> 49:21.166
How can I let you go?

49:29.257 --> 49:30.300
Get ready.

49:30.384 --> 49:31.760
We're going out.

49:45.190 --> 49:47.150
Hyeon-min! Oh!

49:48.902 --> 49:49.903
Are you okay?

49:49.987 --> 49:51.822
-Yeah.
-Are you sure?

49:52.322 --> 49:54.491
I'm doing much better.

49:57.494 --> 49:59.287
I'm so glad to hear that.

50:01.248 --> 50:04.543
How about… your studying.
Are you still at it?

50:08.046 --> 50:09.965
Uh, I don't mean to pressure you.

50:10.048 --> 50:13.635
It's just that the CSATs are coming,
and I'm worried.

50:15.012 --> 50:16.513
You know what I mean, right?

50:17.931 --> 50:18.765
Mm.

50:19.891 --> 50:22.019
Uh, are you comfortable here?

50:22.102 --> 50:23.979
Is the food all right?

50:49.921 --> 50:50.756
Hey, Mom.

50:51.840 --> 50:52.924
Yeah?

50:54.801 --> 50:56.428
There's something I need to tell you.

50:57.137 --> 50:59.097
Tell me. Go ahead.

51:00.515 --> 51:02.059
I'm not taking the CSAT.

51:02.726 --> 51:04.144
And I'm not going to med school.

51:06.354 --> 51:07.230
You're what?

51:07.731 --> 51:09.357
I'll keep studying though.

51:09.858 --> 51:12.277
I'll take the CSAT next year.
I promise you that.

51:14.362 --> 51:16.406
I just can't do it this year.

51:16.907 --> 51:19.201
I don't want to keep living like this.

51:20.410 --> 51:22.829
Just doing what I'm told, without a goal.

51:23.413 --> 51:24.539
I've got

51:25.540 --> 51:28.168
no idea what you're talking about
right now.

51:28.251 --> 51:29.628
Look, Mom…

51:34.800 --> 51:36.885
…even if I don't go to med school,

51:37.469 --> 51:39.096
or take the CSAT…

51:43.016 --> 51:44.601
I'm still your son.

51:46.061 --> 51:46.978
Oh, please--

51:47.062 --> 51:49.815
No matter what I decide,
I hope you'll support me.

51:51.983 --> 51:53.276
No, Hyeon-min.

51:54.694 --> 51:56.530
You're going to med school.

51:57.030 --> 51:58.490
You just have to!

52:08.125 --> 52:09.668
I have to go to treatment now.

52:12.254 --> 52:14.047
Hey. Wait, Hyeon-min!

52:15.006 --> 52:15.882
No!

52:18.093 --> 52:20.595
You really need to stop
sacrificing yourself for me

52:20.679 --> 52:22.973
and start living your own life.

53:17.402 --> 53:21.072
Recent medical tests conducted
in elementary, middle, and high schools,

53:21.156 --> 53:25.327
have revealed that a large number
of students have tested positive

53:25.410 --> 53:28.663
for ADHD drugs
that are not approved for use in Korea.

53:28.747 --> 53:30.957
In several cases, we found a substance

53:31.041 --> 53:34.002
referred to by parents and students
as a "study aid."

53:35.795 --> 53:36.796
This drug,

53:36.880 --> 53:39.758
commonly called "Heart Pill,"

53:39.841 --> 53:43.178
contains ingredients
with narcotic properties.

53:43.803 --> 53:47.057
From this day forward,
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau

53:47.140 --> 53:49.601
will conduct screenings
prior to the CSATs.

53:49.684 --> 53:52.812
Anyone testing positive
will be disqualified.

54:04.366 --> 54:06.243
Are there that many types of drugs?

54:06.868 --> 54:09.246
They look different,
but the ingredients are the same.

54:10.247 --> 54:12.415
These are Full Moon pills.
They were hot ten years ago.

54:12.499 --> 54:14.918
Then, the Snowman ones
were in five years ago.

54:15.001 --> 54:18.129
Here, see this? These markings
were engraved by the dealers.

54:18.213 --> 54:20.340
They're branded, like any other product.

54:20.423 --> 54:21.258
Yeah.

54:22.842 --> 54:25.345
-Two years ago, these were popular.
-Wait…

54:28.306 --> 54:29.891
Could I take a closer look at those?

54:43.989 --> 54:45.907
We're totally fucked, man!

54:47.450 --> 54:48.827
What are we gonna do now?

54:48.910 --> 54:51.871
They shut everything down.
Those stupid fucks at the ERPB.

54:57.711 --> 55:01.423
What do you think?
We just need the ERPB gone, that's all.

55:03.091 --> 55:05.218
WHAT SHOULD I DO… ABOUT GYU-CHEOL?

55:16.980 --> 55:21.609
WILL I EVER BE ABLE TO…
FORGIVE GYU-CHEOL?

55:25.572 --> 55:27.490
CRACKDOWN ON GEN Z-TARGETED
DESIGNER DRUGS

55:35.165 --> 55:38.335
Gyu-cheol,
if your parole hearing goes well

55:38.418 --> 55:42.589
and you're able to be released
back into society, what would you do?

55:43.173 --> 55:45.008
Have you thought about it at all?

55:49.220 --> 55:50.305
I don't know.

55:51.264 --> 55:52.807
I thought I didn't have a chance.

55:54.351 --> 55:57.812
But if I do get out of this place…

56:00.982 --> 56:03.109
I think I'd like to go back to school.

56:05.570 --> 56:08.782
WILL I EVER BE ABLE TO…
FORGIVE GYU-CHEOL?

56:08.865 --> 56:11.159
Based on witness statements
that claim Cho Gyu-cheol

56:11.242 --> 56:13.661
was consistently hostile
toward Ms. Choi Ga-yun,

56:13.745 --> 56:16.414
we are charging the defendant
with premeditated murder

56:16.498 --> 56:19.042
and seeking a sentence
of 15 years in prison.

56:19.876 --> 56:24.297
Clearly, Mr. Cho Gyu-cheol was
changing under Ms. Choi Ga-yun's guidance.

56:24.381 --> 56:28.301
This was nothing more
than an unfortunate accident.

56:43.441 --> 56:44.359
Get on.
